<h1 id="the-problem">The Problem</h1>

<p>Given a 2D grid composed of <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">'1'</code> (land) and <code class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge">'0'</code> (water), count the number of islands in the grid.</p>

<p>An island is always surrounded by water, and each island is formed only by connecting adjacent lands horizontally and/or vertically.</p>

<p>Additionally, you may assume all four edges of the grid are surrounded by water.</p>

